NEARS-1775 — live QA evidence, emulator-5554, com.izzes.nears (UserApp),
Flutter 3.41.9, backend http://10.0.2.2:8000 (local, confirmed up).

All calls below use a scratch copy of scripts/app-nav/uinav.sh with ONLY the
line-671 grep pattern changed to case-insensitive (`grep -aiF` instead of
`grep -aF`) to work around the task_bug (see bug-vm-service-grep-case-mismatch.log)
and prove the rest of the mechanism (pid-bind / forward / getVM / cross-check /
JSON emit / teardown) is sound. This is QA-only, not a repo edit.

=== AC1: one JSON record, pid independently cross-checked ===
$ ui_freshness_probe -s emulator-5554
{"timestamp": "2026-08-20T21:26:56Z", "pid": 20936, "build_symbols": "isolates/4761369954348891"}
$ adb -s emulator-5554 shell pidof com.izzes.nears
20936
-> MATCH.

=== AC2 (same process): two calls, unbroken process ===
$ ui_freshness_probe -s emulator-5554
{"timestamp": "2026-08-20T21:27:04Z", "pid": 20936, "build_symbols": "isolates/4761369954348891"}
$ ui_freshness_probe -s emulator-5554
{"timestamp": "2026-08-20T21:27:04Z", "pid": 20936, "build_symbols": "isolates/4761369954348891"}
-> pid AND build_symbols identical across both calls.

adb forward --list diffed before/after both calls: 0 lines of diff (no leaked
forward entries from either call — teardown confirmed).

=== AC2 (reinstall): new pid, visibly different record ===
